{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2283","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2283","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2283\",\"parent_revision\":\"34c4fc59a67eae8f8e8fa39c25fc8bb28b9dbe1e16ea2659d7392526a145604b\",\"root_revision\":\"34c4fc59a67eae8f8e8fa39c25fc8bb28b9dbe1e16ea2659d7392526a145604b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDuring /dh:implement-feature Pdec8934d, agents T22, T26, and T28 completed their tasks (BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE and INSTRUCTION_UPDATE documentation tasks) and reported STATUS: COMPLETE without committing their changes to git. The swarm-task-planner generated these task definitions with no commit requirement in their requirements, expected-outputs, acceptance-criteria, or verification-steps fields. The only acceptance gate was skilllint exit 0.\\n\\nAs a result, completed work existed on disk but was not recorded in git history. The orchestrator had no documented rule to handle this and had to manually identify and commit the orphaned changes after the fact.\\n\\nObserved at: plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md, complete-implementation/SKILL.md, and multiple agent .md files \u2014 all modified by completed tasks but uncommitted.\\n\\nImpact: git history is incomplete and inconsistent after each implementation wave. Completed task work is invisible in git until manually discovered and committed.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: fix: swarm-task-planner must generate commit step in task acceptance criteria\\nDate: 2026-05-22\\nGoal: Add a Phase 3 rule to swarm-task-planner.md and a template update in generate-task/SKILL.md so that every task whose Expected Outputs lists file paths includes a file-scoped git commit step in Verification Steps, with no Fixes #N trailer.\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n\\nVerified (AVAILABLE):\\n- plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md exists at repo path (696 lines)\\n- Phase 3 rule insertion point is lines 600-611; new rule inserts after line 608 (existing Fixes #N prohibition)\\n- plugins/development-harness/skills/generate-task/SKILL.md exists (105 lines); Verification Steps section at lines 81-83\\n- Same-worktree file-scoped git add constraint documented in groomed Desired Structure section\\n- commit-conventions.md confirmed at plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/commit-conventions.md\\n- Linter gate: uv run prek run --files on both files\\n- Plugin version auto-bump via pre-commit hook confirmed in CLAUDE.md\\n\\nAssumptions to confirm (DERIVABLE):\\n- Commit message format: AC #3 specifies git commit -m \\\"<message>\\\" but exact template not given; derive from commit-conventions.md before writing template text\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:283aa912bfac9362991049891e4da18e -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **swarm-task-planner must generate commit step in task acceptance criteria** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation during /dh:implement-feature Pdec8934d (2026-05-15)\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-16)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Invoke `/dh:add-new-feature` to produce a plan via `swarm-task-planner`.\\\\n2. Ensure the plan includes documentation-only tasks (e.g., BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE, INSTRUCTION_UPDATE task types).\\\\n3. Dispatch one of those tasks via `/dh:implement-feature`.\\\\n4. Observe the agent's task prompt: check `## Acceptance Criteria` and `## Verification Steps` sections.\\\\n5. Agent reports `STATUS: DONE` (or `STATUS: COMPLETE`) without having run `git commit`.\\\\n6. Run `git status` in the working directory \u2014 modified files are present but not committed.\\\\n7. Run `git log --oneline -5` \u2014 no commit was added by the task agent.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- Observed during `/dh:implement-feature Pdec8934d` (2026-05-15): agents T22, T26, T28 completed BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE and INSTRUCTION_UPDATE tasks and reported `STATUS: COMPLETE` with no commit recorded.\\\\n- Files modified: `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md`, `complete-implementation/SKILL.md`, and multiple agent `.md` files.\\\\n- `git log` showed no new commits from these agents. Orphaned changes were discovered and committed manually by the orchestrator after the fact.\\\\n- The generated task prompts contained no commit requirement in `## Requirements`, `## Expected Outputs`, `## Acceptance Criteria`, or `## Verification Steps`.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n9/10 \u2014 P0 classification is correct. Every implementation wave that uses swarm-task-planner risks leaving orphaned changes in the working tree. Git history is the durable audit trail for all agent work; without it, traceability is broken. The bug manifests reliably on any documentation task (BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE, INSTRUCTION_UPDATE) and potentially on any non-code task that lacks an explicit commit step.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: reliable git history across all feature implementation waves using swarm-task-planner.\\\\n- Bottleneck: the orchestrator in `/dh:implement-feature` has no rule to handle uncommitted task output \u2014 it must manually identify and commit orphaned changes (observed in Pdec8934d).\\\\n- Affects: all task types where the only acceptance gate is a linter exit code (e.g., `skilllint exit 0`), with no commit step.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Each completed task leaves exactly one commit in git history, making agent work traceable and auditable.\\\\n- Orchestrators no longer need to discover and commit orphaned files after the fact.\\\\n- The `git log` health-check in `implement-feature` (no new commits when implementation work should be in progress) becomes meaningful \u2014 absence of a commit signals a real problem, not a missing task requirement.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen swarm-task-planner generates a task whose expected output includes modified or created files, the generated task's `## Acceptance Criteria` and/or `## Verification Steps` include a step requiring the agent to commit its changes to git before reporting done. The commit step must follow the `Fixes #N` restriction: task-level commits must not include `Fixes #N`, `Closes #N`, or `Resolves #N` trailers. After the fix, `git log` shows a new commit for each completed task that modified files.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe `swarm-task-planner` agent's Phase 3 (Task Decomposition) rules (in `agents/swarm-task-planner.md` lines 596\u2013608) include an explicit rule: every task whose `## Expected Outputs` lists file paths must include a commit step in `## Verification Steps`. The rule must reference the existing `Fixes #N` prohibition already at line 605.\\\\n\\\\nThe same constraint propagates to `/dh:generate-task` SKILL.md, which generates individual task prompts. The task template's `## Verification Steps` section adds a commit step whenever `## Expected Outputs` is non-empty.\\\\n\\\\nThe generated commit step must scope `git add` to the files listed in `## Expected Outputs` (not `git add .` or `git add -A`) to prevent cross-task staging pollution when multiple agents write to the same worktree concurrently. This is the same-worktree safety constraint. In isolated-worktree mode the agent can commit freely, but using file-scoped `git add` is safe in both modes.\\\\n\\\\nNote: the source file to edit is in the working plugin directory `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md`, not the cache path. The plugin version bumps automatically via the pre-commit hook on commit.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Open `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` Phase 3 rules \u2014 a rule exists stating every task whose `## Expected Outputs` lists one or more file paths MUST include a `git commit` step in `## Verification Steps`.\\\\n2. Open `plugins/development-harness/skills/generate-task/SKILL.md` \u2014 the task template's `## Verification Steps` section includes a commit step when `## Expected Outputs` is non-empty.\\\\n3. Generate a documentation task (e.g., BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE or INSTRUCTION_UPDATE) via swarm-task-planner \u2014 the generated task contains a `## Verification Steps` entry that runs `git add <output files> && git commit -m \\\"<message>\\\"` with no `Fixes #N` trailer.\\\\n4. The generated commit step specifies the exact files from `## Expected Outputs`, not `git add .` or `git add -A`, to prevent cross-task staging pollution in same-worktree mode.\\\\n5. Run `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md plugins/development-harness/skills/generate-task/SKILL.md` \u2014 linter exits 0.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\\\n|------|------|\\\\n| Agent | swarm-task-planner \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` (source); cached at `7.12.18/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` |\\\\n| Skill | `/dh:generate-task` \u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/generate-task/SKILL.md` |\\\\n| Skill | `/dh:clear-cove-task-design` \u2014 CLEAR+CoVe task writing standard; defines Verification Steps section |\\\\n| Skill | `/dh:start-task` \u2014 already documents `Fixes #N` prohibition at step 6 (lines 159\u2013165 in cache) |\\\\n| Reference | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/commit-conventions.md` \u2014 `Fixes #N` restriction rule |\\\\n| Prior work | swarm-task-planner.md Phase 3 rules lines 596\u2013608 \u2014 location of the gap and the fix |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 independently fixable.\\\\n- Blocks: None directly; companion item #2282 (implement-feature skill missing commit ownership documentation for same-worktree vs isolated-worktree execution) covers the orchestrator-side documentation. Both items address the same Pdec8934d incident from different angles and can be fixed in parallel.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Execution-mode nuance: same-worktree mode requires file-scoped `git add <files>` rather than `git add .` in the generated commit step, to prevent an agent from staging another agent's in-progress changes. This must be reflected in the template. The orchestrator-side rule for this is tracked in #2282.\\\\n- Verify the source file path before editing: confirm `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` exists in the working repo (not just the plugin cache) before applying the fix.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the fix is a targeted addition of one rule to Phase 3 of `swarm-task-planner.md` and a corresponding template update in `generate-task/SKILL.md`. No schema changes, no new test fixtures required. Linter validation (`uv run prek run --files`) is the primary verification gate.\\n\",\"digest\":\"ab91e0fc5ec4ba61e9bd48eb43e5421f89d97f7ef3ac3f938d99b9797add9bae\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCQRuw\"}"}